      "actualInertWitness": "parse_stat(b108 (node) S 1 +17 zero fields +123 LF,108) returned a proof; explicit must-refuse assertion failed.",
      "correction": "Validate a complete fixed kernel stat grammar/count and one terminal LF, preserving all raw bytes and numeric precision. Bind supported full-record shape to actual observed kernel/proc source; do not merely increase a guessed threshold. Update synthetic positive fixtures to full records and keep truncation/extra-tail/duplicate-line negatives.",
      "documentaryKnownFullShape": {
        "postCommFieldCount": 50,
        "qualification": "Existing actual PID1 full-record observation is source-shape grounding only, not fresh keeper05/Node proof.",
        "raw": {
          "bytes": 270,
          "path": "scratch/r22-adoption-161/public-installer-preparation/populated-history-process-fence-diagnostic-01/inspector-runner-birth-01/actual-capture-01/04-pid1-stat-before.stdout.raw",
          "sha256": "sha256:04cdbb8fbdd0df704c38720362824faeb1bae432f4baed92c81e68aaec737693"
        }
      },
      "finding": "Accepts truncation at20 post-comm fields, immediately after startTicks. This violates full nontruncated raw stat requirement; the original positive stat fixture itself has that truncated shape.",
      "id": "I1",
      "source": "run_external_process_once.py:parse_stat"
    },
    {
      "actualInertWitness": "Original caller helper authority changed c*64 to d*64 between proofs; attest_after accepted and explicit must-refuse assertion failed.",
      "correction": "Capture an immutable type-preserving canonical helper-authority snapshot/fingerprint at construction, validate it and bind both proof phases to the same admitted bytes. Reject mutations/changed order or adopt one explicit canonical order; carry the fixed authority digest into each attestation and revalidate against the source/permit authority.",
      "finding": "Stores helper_authority by mutable reference. After pre-proof, mutation of all authority exe hashes with matching altered post helper tuples is accepted; the two attestations can bind different helper authorities.",
      "id": "I2",
      "source": "run_external_process_once.py:PureRendezvous.__init__/attest_after"
    }
  ],
